  "method": "One OKLCH ladder, measured from Lagoon, shared by every theme. Each token has a fixed lightness and chroma (e.g. dark bg L .171 C .012, surface .215/.014, raised .259/.018, overlay .275/.019, line .299/.021, border .534/.025, text .945/.010, muted .718/.022, glass-tint .211/.019, primary .766/.127, primary-hover = primary-text = focus .803/.121, on-primary .221/.035, primary-soft .263/.033; light bg .971/.003, raised .945/.006, line .897/.010, border .622/.023, text .215/.020, muted .461/.023, glass-tint .985/.003, primary = focus .522/.090, primary-hover = primary-text .469/.081, primary-soft .952/.021, surface = overlay = on-primary = #ffffff). A theme is a set of seeds: primary hue hp (optionally hp_light), neutral hue hn, accent family (brand amber, or Lagoon teal when the primary is warm), chroma multipliers set by eye (nc_dark, nc_light for neutrals; pc_dark, pc_light for the primary), and hue offsets for any semantic colour that would sit within 28 degrees of the primary. Hues: bg/surface/raised/overlay/line use hn; border, muted, glass-tint and all light neutrals use hn moved 1/4 of the way to hp; dark text uses the midpoint; primary-soft uses hp moved 1/5 of the way to hn. Colours outside sRGB are brought in by reducing chroma only. A solver then raises or lowers lightness until every WCAG 2.1 pair passes (it had nothing to do for these seeds). True black replaces bg with #000000 and drops surface/raised/overlay/line/glass-tint to L .145/.195/.215/.255/.130 at the same hue and chroma. Lagoon is kept verbatim from kiboto-brand-tokens.css; the generator reproduces it within OKLab dE 0.005. display = dark bg (dark) or text (light); display-glow = dark primary-text. glass-tint is new: the colour laid over the wallpaper at --glass-opacity.",
  "default": "lagoon",
  "modes": [
    "light",
    "dark",
    "auto"
  ],
